<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15044" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀριθμ-ητός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that can be counted,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					153
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.145
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠριθμημένον ἢ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					223a24
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετρητόν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1020a9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>easily numbered, few in number,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀριθμητοὺς ἀπὸ πολλῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					16.87
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀ.</span>
			<i>of</i> no <i>account,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				14.48
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
